# All device kinds (default scope)

Keep in sync with `~/.cursor/rules/all-device-kinds.mdc` when that file changes.

When the human talks about Zigbee (or mixed) devices missing commands, group/automation bursts, delivery, retries, pacing, or “not all devices received the command”:

- Default scope is **ALL device kinds** (On/Off, covering, write-attr, cluster commands, multi-endpoint / multi-channel, and any other command path in the same radio/control stack) — not only On/Off switchers.
- NEVER propose, design, or implement a fix that applies **only** to On/Off (or any other single kind) unless the human **explicitly** says to limit the change to that kind.
- Examples of group/channel talk (“4 relays”, “4 channels of the same device”) are still **all kinds** unless they name a kind restriction.
- Do not offer “On/Off-only” options as the default path; if a kind-limited option exists, label it clearly as scoped and only use it after an explicit human choice.
